## 5. THE STACK (and why each choice)

| Layer | Technology | Why |
|---|---|---|
| **Frontend** | React 18 + Vite + TypeScript | Fast, standard, huge ecosystem |
| **Styling** | Custom CSS (index.css) | Full brand control, no framework overhead |
| **Routing** | React Router 6 | Standard SPA routing |
| **API** | Hono (TypeScript) | Runtime-agnostic — runs on Workers, Node, Bun, Deno, Azure |
| **Worker runtime** | Cloudflare Workers | Free tier, global edge, integrated with Pages |
| **Database** | Supabase Postgres (Sydney) | Real Postgres, AU residency, free tier |
| **ORM** | Drizzle | Type-safe, portable to any Postgres |
| **Postgres driver** | `postgres` (porsager) | Works in both Node AND Workers (unlike `pg`) |
| **Connection pooling** | Cloudflare Hyperdrive | Required for Workers → external Postgres |
| **Frontend hosting** | Cloudflare Pages | Free static hosting |
| **Proxy layer** | Pages Functions | Bridges browser ↔ Worker (no CORS drama) |
| **Testing** | Playwright (UI) + Node fetch (API) | Headless Chrome for real interaction tests |
| **Source control** | GitHub (`ntchita/helphome`) | Standard |

**Why this specific combination:**
- **Hono** was chosen because the same code runs on Cloudflare Workers today and Azure tomorrow (only the adapter changes).
- **`postgres` driver** instead of `pg` because `pg` doesn't work in Workers (no TCP).
- **Hyperdrive** because Workers can't hold raw Postgres connections — Hyperdrive pools them.
- **Supabase** because it's the closest free-tier to Azure Postgres we'll eventually migrate to — no code changes needed, just a new connection string.

