## 6. THE ARCHITECTURE
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ BROWSER (desktop / mobile) │
└──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┘
│ HTTPS
▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ CLOUDFLARE PAGES (helphome-app.pages.dev) │
│ ├── React SPA (compiled from src/frontend/) │
│ └── Pages Function (functions/api/[[path]].ts) │
│ → forwards /api/* to the Worker │
└──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┘
│ HTTPS (server-to-server)
▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ CLOUDFLARE WORKER (helphome-api.lifewealth.workers.dev) │
│ Hono API — all business logic │
│ ├── Auth middleware (x-user-id header) │
│ ├── Role guards (client/worker/coordinator/admin) │
│ └── 30+ routes (see §8) │
└──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┘
│ Hyperdrive binding
▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ SUPABASE POSTGRES (Sydney, ap-southeast-2) │
│ 14 tables, multi-tenant via tenant_id │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

**Why the proxy layer exists:**
Without it, the browser would need to hit the Worker directly from a different origin, requiring careful CORS config on every request. With the proxy:
- Browser sees only `helphome-app.pages.dev`
- No CORS in the browser (same-origin)
- Proxy forwards to the Worker with clean headers
- Worker sees a plain server-to-server call

**Security boundary:**
- Browser NEVER talks to Supabase directly
- Supabase password exists only in two places: local `.dev.vars` and Cloudflare Worker secret
- All data access goes through the Worker (which enforces role guards)

